The idea: You're a thief sneaking through a dark museum, and you can't see anything. The only way to "see" is to tap and send out a sound wave. The wave reveals the walls, guards, and treasure for a split second, then fades.

The twist: Every wave also tells the guards where you are. So every tap is a gamble between knowing where you are and being heard.

How it plays:

Tap to send out an echo that shows the room around you.
Swipe to move quietly. Moving slowly is silent, and moving fast makes noise.
Grab the glowing treasure, then reach the exit.
Guards walk patrols and rush toward any sound they hear.
You can throw a coin to make noise somewhere else and pull the guards away.
